yippee-ki-yay movie lovers it's Jan here  Marvel's latest movie Doctor Strange  takes us into a world of dazzling new  dimensions and amazing magical powers  that look truly extraordinary up on the  big screen over the course of the film  director scott derrickson leads us  creatively through a wealth of  exceptionally striking wildly out-there  images of fantastical events and I think  this so he sometimes draws in intriguing  ways on his background as a writer and  director of horror movies like the  consistently creepy sinister in fact for  both the characters and the audience the  movie's visuals and action scenes  frequently blur the lines between waking  nightmare dream and hallucination the  movie manages to literally upend action  genre tropes like one foot chases and  ticking clock scenarios and gives them a  nicely inventive spin to create totally  trippy whacked-out sequences forget your  boring old laws of physics in dr.  strange practically and if it goes  streets buildings walls ceilings floors  and more bend forwards backwards and in  on one another and turn upside down and  twist around in constant motion yes  there are inception and matrix-style  moments but there's so much more than  that Doctor Strange is a wondrous world  of mind-bending movement coupled with a  kaleidoscope of fractured shapes and  colors that send us hurtling through  different dimensions there are even  times in this Steve Ditko inspired  psychedelic world when you actually feel  like you're looking at a moving comic  book page the visuals are so spectacular  and there's so much going on in them at  the same time that it's almost hard to  know where to look in fact it's such a  feast for your eyes that it's a movie  were seeing more than once on the big  screen and just like Jon Favreau's  live-action Jungle Book Doctor Strange  as a movie that really does reap the  rewards of 3d scott derrickson and his  super skilled visual effects teams have  clearly gone all out to make the very  most of that technology and it shows and  on the visual side I've got to give  credit to production designer Charles  wood and the movies art direction and  set decoration teams for creating  beautifully detailed sets including Hong  Kong Street New York homes and Kamata  then of course there's the movies actors  and what a captivating cast Marvel's  managed to assemble for Doctor Strange  obviously we already knew that Benedict  Cumberbatch could play a charming  arrogant genius in a sleep we are  talking after all about the man who  Sherlock Holmes to 21st century life to  such well-deserved critical acclaim and  he does an equally top-notch job as a  self-important neurosurgeon Stephen  strange yes Doctor Strange is a role  that fits Cumberbatch like a glove just  as was the case with Iron Man and Robert  Downey jr. you'll doubtless remember  that there was a good deal of  controversy over the casting of Tilda  Swinton in the role of the ancient one  given the characters an Asian man in the  comics focusing solely on their  performance in the film though Swinton  manages to be ethereal badass and  sharply witty often all at once even  when she's having to explain so much of  the Ruby's mythology Chiwetel Ejiofor  brings poison a certain class the  character of Mordo who studied under the  ancient one and whose function in the  film is too often exposition by tweaking  the comic book role of Christine Palmer  played by Rachel McAdams the movie  quietly acknowledges that if you're a  woman working in a hospital you may  actually be a doctor not a nurse however  the character of Palmer as it's written  isn't particularly scintillating and  it's a testament to the talents of  McAdams that she makes the part work  giving Palmer a level of emotional depth  as the Benedict Wong's character Wong he  gets a welcome makeover from the comics  so instead of being dr. strangers  manservant he's now a steely rule  enforcing librarian at Kumar Taj the  scenes the to Benedict's sure together  are a treat and I'd love to see more of  them just like the rest of the cast Mads  Mikkelsen is an incredible actor but as  the movies baddie Kai Caelius the script  doesn't give him enough opportunity or  on-screen time to connect with us sure  he gets to be part of some cool visually  stunning scenes but in terms of dialogue  and motivation it's pretty thin stuff  having said that where Mickelson does  appear on screen it's still always a  pleasure to see him I just hope his role  in row one is more worthy if it's acting  talents this being a Marvel movie you  can expect a good deal of comedy as is  often the case with any comedy some of  it works while some doesn't land for me  the better comic moments come from the  interaction between the two Benedict's  Tilda Swinton's at times almost  gleefully winking ancient one and dr.  strangers cloak of levitation which is a  playful air of Aladdin's magic carpet  meets baby Groot about it though let's  face it it's hard for anything to outdo  a talking dancing tree as you may have  gathered from everything I said so far  sadly Doctor Strange his script doesn't  live up to the promise of its  spellbinding visual design and its  incredible cast were 14 films into the  all cinematic universe now and I guess  unsurprisingly in some ways dr.  Strange's story feels more than a tad  familiar in fact we've almost come full  circle back to 2008 iron man movie is  this latest film basically follows Tony  Stark's character arc of course is  always a certain amount of been there  done that in any superhero origin story  and perhaps there was a sense among the  script writers and producers that the  outrageously off-kilter reality of this  movies world was more than enough to  make it different or maybe they thought  at that stunningly surreal world that  it's bizarre mythology was already more  than enough for the audience to cope  with without adding further deviations  from the already well-worn origin story  route and to an extent they're right on  both counts  after all the film's dizzying visuals do  make it stand out from Marvel's other  movies and there's so much head spinning  craziness and dr. strangers story that  have been rather a tall order to do what  silver warded so well for Black Panther  and the admittedly already well-known  Spider Man and just plunk strange in the  middle of Avengers infinity war without  giving him a proper feature-length  introduction like this one however with  a stronger more daring script and  derrickson and see Robert Cargill who  worked together on sinister and their  co-writer John Speights Doctor Strange  could have been one of Marvel's very  best movies ever  still this Doctor Strange movie does  show much promise for future outings of  the master of the mystic arts and if  Marvel keeps up this level of i popping  imagery and finesses the scripts were in  for one hell of a trippy ride in later  installments  by the way Doctor Strange is such a  standalone film that you can even enjoy  it without having seen a single Marvel  movie or TV show that said there are  easter eggs and references in there for  fans of Marvel's wider work on the big  screen and in the comic books though  I've gotta say there's been so many  brilliant Stan Lee cameos that this one  kiyah pales somewhat in comparison to  sum up Doctor Strange is a dizzying  dazzling visual delight with stellar  work from the design art costume and  effects departments and the scott  derrickson is capable directions and the  wonderfully accomplished car squeeze the  very most out of the scripts predictable  plotting and reams of exposition Doctor  Strange gets three and a half out of 5  flicks now what did you think of Doctor  Strange have you seen it already  or what are you most looking forward to  about the film and how do you feel it  compares to Marvel's other movies I look  forward to reading your comments below  I've got videos coming up explaining the  post-credits and Doctor Strange and my  full guide to all the movies Easter eggs  click on the links below to check those  out if you enjoyed this video do please  like share and subscribe thanks for  watching and see you next time you'll be  going movie lovers
 

